rm=\"translate(771,-309.4) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> "}],"correct_options":["A","B","C","D"],"explanation":"<p>When connected by a wire, charges on A and B are redistributed until potential on both becomes equal. After the charge redistribution, A and B are not influenced by each other because they are far apart. Thus, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.749ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.577ex\" height=\"2.681ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -853.7 4675 1184.8\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(848.3,363) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D456\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D456\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(345,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(945,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D460\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D460\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1414,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D456\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D456\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1759,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2282,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D452\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D452\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(771,-331.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3119.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(4175,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> as field inside a conducting shell is zero.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l4k39xk7/051c6a39-3597-4a18-a55e-a40d65bff0bd/f80eaa80-ef22-11ec-af85-e5c347851f91/file-1l4k39xk8.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l4k39xk7/051c6a39-3597-4a18-a55e-a40d65bff0bd/f80eaa80-ef22-11ec-af85-e5c347851f91/file-1l4k39xk8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Electrostatics Question 62 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l4k39xk7/051c6a39-3597-4a18-a55e-a40d65bff0bd/f80eaa80-ef22-11ec-af85-e5c347851f91/file-1l4k39xk8.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l4k39xk7/051c6a39-3597-4a18-a55e-a40d65bff0bd/f80eaa80-ef22-11ec-af85-e5c347851f91/file-1l4k39xk8.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l4k39xk7/051c6a39-3597-4a18-a55e-a40d65bff0bd/f80eaa80-ef22-11ec-af85-e5c347851f91/file-1l4k39xk8.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l4k39xk7/051c6a39-3597-4a18-a55e-a40d65bff0bd/f80eaa80-ef22-11ec-af85-e5c347851f91/file-1l4k39xk8.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l4k39xk7/051c6a39-3597-4a18-a55e-a40d65bff0bd/f80eaa80-ef22-11ec-af85-e5c347851f91/file-1l4k39xk8.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l4k39xk7/051c6a39-3597-4a18-a55e-a40d65bff0bd/f80eaa80-ef22-11ec-af85-e5c347851f91/file-1l4k39xk8.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>So choice (a) is correct.</p>\n<p>Let Q<sub>A</sub> and Q<sub>B</sub> are the charges on metal shell A and metal sphere B after they are connected by a wire. Since t